<task id="035" project="spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Review Policy Question (submit question → official human answer via feedback loop) + Policy Library browse/read</title>
    <phase>P3 Legal Front Door intake MVP</phase>
    <gate>blocked-until:031,034</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Client (Fluent v9) + BFF read/submit surface spanning the Front Door group; consumes 034's grid config + 030's feedback fields; tags frontend/bff-api — FULL per CLAUDE.md §8.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Well-specified composition — a PolicyQuestion request type on the 031 framework + the FR-24 feedback loop + the 034 Policy Library grid; no new architecture, reuses established seams.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Consumes 031 (intake framework) + 034 (grid config + governance schema) + 030 (feedback fields); touches the shared external-access BFF surface; sequential after its deps.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>031,034</deps>
    <tags>frontend, bff-api</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>
  <prompt>Build the FR-25 read side: (1) "Review Policy Question" — a PolicyQuestion Front Door request type on the 031 intake framework where a user submits a policy question and receives an OFFICIAL HUMAN answer from the law department (NOT AI — that's FR-26) via the FR-24 feedback loop (legal answers in the MDA; the answer returns to the requester in-app + email); (2) the Policy Library browse/read surface — a widget rendering the 034 Policy Library sprk_gridconfiguration (entity=sprk_document, filter category=Policy + published) read-only via BffDataverseClient, with document read/open. Reuse the 031 framework + 030 feedback fields + 034 grid; do NOT build a new grid or a new feedback path.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Fluent v9 + React 18 on @spaarke/ui-components + the DataGrid framework; ASP.NET Minimal API endpoint groups (ADR-008/019) for any read/submit route on the Front Door group; app-only broker reads (ADR-028/A3, no OBO).</role>
  <goal>A workforce Front Door user can: (1) submit a PolicyQuestion request through the 031 intake framework and later see the law department's official human answer (decision/response text + response docs) rendered on their my-requests detail + emailed — via the FR-24 loop (030 fields; 037 renders the shared feedback); (2) browse/read the Policy Library — a widget backed by the 034 sprk_gridconfiguration (category=Policy + published) reading read-only via BffDataverseClient, and open/read a policy document (app-only, no Power-Apps license). Expired/unpublished policies never surface (034 governance trim). No new grid, no new feedback path.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-25 (spec.md line 257): R2 builds both (i) a browse/read policy library and (ii) "Review Policy Question" — a user submits a policy question and receives an official HUMAN response from the law department (NOT an AI answer — that's FR-26). "Review Policy Question" is a Front Door request type (PolicyQuestion) that reuses the intake (031) + the FR-24 official-human-response feedback loop (legal answers in the MDA; the answer returns to the requester in-app + email — 037 renders it). The library home reuses sprk_document category=Policy (034) + governance fields + the existing indexing lifecycle. Two read roles kept separate: (a) grounding — Ask Legal policy_search (FR-26/051) hits the AI-Search policy index (NOT this task); (b) browse — the Policy Library grid reads sprk_document via sprk_gridconfiguration + BffDataverseClient (THIS task). Both filter published/effective. Authoring is by law-dept core users in the MDA — the external portal is READ-ONLY on P&amp;P. This task delivers the PolicyQuestion request-type registration + the browse/read widget; the feedback RENDER is shared with 037 (FR-24).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/spec.md (FR-25 line 257 — Review Policy Question + browse/read; FR-24 feedback loop)</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/tasks/031-typed-intake-framework.poml (the intake framework + request-type registry to register PolicyQuestion into)</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/tasks/034-pnp-document-architecture.poml (the Policy Library sprk_gridconfiguration + governance schema this browse surface consumes)</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/tasks/030-servicerequest-intake-schema.poml (sprk_requesttype=PolicyQuestion + the decision/response feedback fields)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DataGrid/** + docs/guides/DATAGRID-FRAMEWORK-CONFIGURATION-GUIDE.md (&lt;DataGrid configId=…&gt; + BffDataverseClient read-only broker — the browse surface)</file>
      <file>src/client/external-spa/** (the module-host shell + the 031 driver to register PolicyQuestion + mount the Policy Library widget)</file>
      <file>docs/standards/MODAL-DECISION-CRITERIA.md + MODAL-DESIGN-SYSTEM.md (open/read a policy document via the right modal preset)</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md (binding BFF governance — Placement Justification + publish size)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>031 (intake framework + request-type registry) — PolicyQuestion registers as a request type. 034 (sprk_documentcategory + governance fields + Policy Library sprk_gridconfiguration + governance trim) — the browse surface reads this grid. 030 (feedback fields decision/response) — the official-human answer writes here; 037 renders the shared feedback (this task registers PolicyQuestion + browse; the feedback render is 037).</dependencies>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">"Review Policy Question" MUST be a PolicyQuestion request type on the 031 intake framework (config/schema + a form) — do NOT build a bespoke question flow or a new endpoint group. The answer is an OFFICIAL HUMAN response via the FR-24 loop (legal answers in the MDA) — NOT an AI answer (that is FR-26/051; do not add AI here).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The Policy Library browse surface MUST render the 034 sprk_gridconfiguration (entity=sprk_document, filter category=Policy + published) via &lt;DataGrid configId=…&gt; + BffDataverseClient read-only — do NOT hand-roll a grid or add a new read endpoint. External is read-only on P&amp;P (authoring is MDA-side).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Expired/unpublished policies MUST NOT surface in the browse grid — rely on the 034 governance trim (published/effective filter). Verify with a negative case.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">All reads are app-only broker (no OBO) — the external caller token authenticates only to the BFF; Dataverse/SPE reads are app-only, entitlement-scoped.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent v9 semantic tokens only; zero hardcoded hex; verified light/dark/Teams theme + narrow Teams personal-tab width; document open/read via @spaarke/ui-components modal presets (no hand-rolled Dialog, §11/ADR-050).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Any BFF read/submit addition: state the Placement Justification in the PR (cite .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md); report dotnet publish size delta vs baseline 46.90 MB (ceiling ≤60 MB); run /conflict-check before the BFF PR. (Most of this task is client + config; flag if no BFF change is needed.)</constraint>
  </constraints>
