  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Load spec.md FR-25 (line 257) + FR-24 + ux-brief + the DataGrid framework docs + 031/034/030 task files. Run /conflict-check if a BFF change is needed.</step>
    <step order="2">Register PolicyQuestion as a request type in the 031 intake framework (config + a question form via WizardModal/FormModal). Submit writes a sprk_servicerequest (requesttype=PolicyQuestion) via the existing Front Door group — no new endpoint group.</step>
    <step order="3">Confirm the FR-24 loop covers PolicyQuestion: legal's official human answer (decision/response text + response docs) is written MDA-side into the 030 feedback fields; the requester sees it in-app (my-requests, rendered by 037) + email (037). This task ensures PolicyQuestion flows through that shared loop — do NOT build a separate answer path or any AI answer.</step>
    <step order="4">Build the Policy Library browse/read widget: render the 034 sprk_gridconfiguration (entity=sprk_document, filter category=Policy + published) via &lt;DataGrid configId=…&gt; + BffDataverseClient read-only; wire document open/read via a modal preset. Mount as a role-defaulted widget in the shell.</step>
    <step order="5">Implement the required states (loading, empty, error, unentitled/denied, dark, Teams theme, keyboard, narrow width) per ux-brief §4 for both the PolicyQuestion form and the Policy Library grid.</step>
    <step order="6">Tests: client component tests for the PolicyQuestion form (renders through the 031 driver) + the Policy Library grid (renders the config; expired/unpublished excluded — negative). If a BFF change exists, add KEEP-path integration tests (no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;/DI/ctor tests, ADR-038).</step>
    <step order="7">Build: npm run build:prod (client); if BFF changed, dotnet publish -c Release + report size delta vs 46.90 MB + Placement Justification.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅ completed.</step>
    <step order="9">Document any deviations in projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>
  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build/test the external-spa client (build:prod)</tool>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build/test/publish the BFF if a read/submit change is needed</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Shell, /conflict-check</tool>
  </tools>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/external-spa/** — PolicyQuestion request type registered in the 031 framework + a Policy Library browse/read widget (&lt;DataGrid configId=…&gt; + BffDataverseClient)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/** — client component tests for the PolicyQuestion form + Policy Library grid (published-only negative); BFF KEEP-path tests only if a BFF change exists</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the Front Door, when a user opens "Review Policy Question", then a PolicyQuestion form renders through the 031 intake framework (config + a form, no framework change) and submit creates a sprk_servicerequest with requesttype=PolicyQuestion.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a submitted PolicyQuestion, when legal writes an official human answer (decision/response) MDA-side, then it returns to the requester via the FR-24 loop (in-app my-requests + email, rendered by 037) — NOT an AI answer.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the Policy Library widget, when it loads, then it renders the 034 sprk_gridconfiguration (entity=sprk_document, filter category=Policy) via &lt;DataGrid configId=…&gt; + BffDataverseClient read-only — no hand-rolled grid in the diff.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given an unpublished or expired policy, when the Policy Library grid loads, then it never appears (034 governance trim / published filter).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a policy row, when the user opens it, then the document reads via a modal preset app-only (no OBO, no Power-Apps license, no Graph pointer exposure).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given both surfaces, when rendered in light/dark/Teams theme at narrow width, then semantic tokens adapt with zero hardcoded hex and no console errors.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Policy Library browse + read">
      <steps><step>Open the Policy Library widget in the shell</step><step>Verify published policies list; open one to read</step></steps>
      <expected>Grid renders the 034 config via BffDataverseClient; document opens in a modal preset; expired/unpublished absent; no console errors</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Review Policy Question submit">
      <steps><step>Open "Review Policy Question"</step><step>Fill + submit the question form</step></steps>
      <expected>Form renders through the 031 driver; a PolicyQuestion sprk_servicerequest is created; confirmation shown</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark + Teams theme (ADR-021)">
      <steps><step>Toggle dark mode; load inside a Teams-theme host at narrow width</step></steps>
      <expected>Zero hardcoded hex; tokens adapt across light/dark/Teams; readable at Teams personal-tab width</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>
  <notes>Spec FR-25 (line 257) read side + FR-24. Review Policy Question = a PolicyQuestion request type on the 031 framework → OFFICIAL HUMAN answer via the FR-24 loop (NOT AI — AI Q&amp;A is FR-26/051). Policy Library browse reuses the 034 grid config + BffDataverseClient (read-only; external is read-only on P&amp;P). Feedback RENDER (in-app + email) is shared with 037. No new grid, no new feedback path, no AI. Use build:prod per CLAUDE.md §12 / AP-1.</notes>
